/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 9 grids in Potter County came in under 90% of normal for October to November in 45 of 75 years since 1951. In 2025, April to May ran 182% of normal on the middle of the grids, and October to November fell to 67% in 2025. In 2026 so far, February to March came in at 8% and March to April at 18% on the middle of the grids. Every grid had its driest year in 2011, with grid 18114 at 38%.</p>"}
